WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.612
Search housing across four locked OKF
source snapshots.

2
00:00:03.892 --> 00:00:06.757
The results include A Life in the UK and
ONS.

3
00:00:07.037 --> 00:00:11.620
They include UK Government APIs and
metadata-only HM Land Registry.

4
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.451
This is an independent prototype, not a
government service.

5
00:00:15.731 --> 00:00:19.142
The ordering shows bounded relevance, not
a trust score.

6
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:22.178
Evidence Trace puts evidence before
answers.

7
00:00:22.458 --> 00:00:25.863
Eighty reviewed records retain item-level
evidence receipts.

8
00:00:26.143 --> 00:00:31.243
Another 58,652 records support wider
governed discovery.

9
00:00:31.523 --> 00:00:35.851
They come from 58,655 locked source rows.

10
00:00:36.131 --> 00:00:39.421
Three standalone legislation rows remain
quarantined.

11
00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:43.518
This result keeps its collection and
checksum-bound snapshot visible.

12
00:00:43.798 --> 00:00:46.797
Its source link has the
producer-declared-source role.

13
00:00:47.077 --> 00:00:50.442
The destination hostname and limitations
remain inspectable.

14
00:00:50.722 --> 00:00:53.695
Source authority is not independently
established.

15
00:00:53.975 --> 00:00:56.956
This wider tier does not claim an
item-level receipt.

16
00:00:57.236 --> 00:01:01.413
This reconstruction names the host,
version and observation time.

17
00:01:01.693 --> 00:01:05.354
Its receipt records all five native page
tools and their schemas.

18
00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:09.025
Search uses the same housing query and
four collections.

19
00:01:09.305 --> 00:01:12.756
Record and provenance calls use the bound
federated result.

20
00:01:13.036 --> 00:01:16.742
Reviewed tools explore and compare
separate evidence facets.

21
00:01:17.022 --> 00:01:20.782
The page accepts no personal-context field
and hosts no model.

22
00:01:21.062 --> 00:01:25.065
This receipt proves host invocation; no
model selected a tool.

23
00:01:25.345 --> 00:01:28.668
Reviewed evidence supports a deeper,
receipt-bound view.

24
00:01:28.948 --> 00:01:32.002
People and agents can inspect one answer
foundation.

25
00:01:32.282 --> 00:01:36.392
They can compare authority, freshness,
integrity and rights.

26
00:01:36.672 --> 00:01:39.310
Access and coverage remain separate as
well.

27
00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.774
No combined score hides uncertainty or
declares a winner.

28
00:01:43.054 --> 00:01:46.819
A fresh manual Safari and VoiceOver
journey checks this release.

29
00:01:47.099 --> 00:01:51.340
It follows headings, controls, search and
the selected record.

30
00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:55.408
It checks the source-link role,
destination and authority label.

31
00:01:55.688 --> 00:01:59.929
It also covers comparison, live status and
focus restoration.

32
00:02:00.209 --> 00:02:04.328
This bounded observation is not a WCAG
conformance claim.

33
00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.985
This page hosts no model, profile or chat
history.

34
00:02:08.265 --> 00:02:13.072
Your AI sends declared arguments;
providers may receive prompts and results.

35
00:02:13.352 --> 00:02:16.473
The static path calls no official API or
model.

36
00:02:16.753 --> 00:02:20.598
Land Registry stays metadata-only, without
personal rows.

37
00:02:20.878 --> 00:02:24.596
No searchable legislation collection or
result link is published.

38
00:02:24.876 --> 00:02:28.943
No legislation request occurs;
cross-references stay inert.

39
00:02:29.223 --> 00:02:32.516
Privacy, cost and accuracy remain
hypotheses.

40
00:02:32.796 --> 00:02:35.689
Your AI asks. You inspect the evidence.
